@hauntsaninja, I couldn't reproduce the issue directly, but it occurs when using OpenFL while running the taskrunner workspace for torch/mnist (https://openfl.readthedocs.io/en/latest/tutorials/taskrunner.html#).

@poedator, I was able to resolve the issue with pip version 24.1.2 without the patch.

For details please refer https://github.com/securefederatedai/openfl/issues/1441.

issues.body:
We should audit places in Dynamo where we assert/internal error, and if these can be triggered from user code, we should change them to graph breaks or raise an observed exception.

For example:
```python
import torch


@torch.compile(backend="eager")
def fn(x):
    return x + 1, "\n".join("a", "b")


fn(torch.ones(3))
```

gives hard error:
```
  File "/data/users/williamwen/pytorch/torch/_dynamo/variables/constant.py", line 148, in call_method
    assert len(args) == 1 and len(kwargs) == 0
           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
AssertionError: 

from user code:
   File "/data/users/williamwen/pytorch/playground3.py", line 6, in fn
    return x + 1, "\n".join("a", "b")
```

